  reason: "The required floor's stale-match planning (gunbc#11194) needs the base revision's declaration index reconstructed from the head index with the diff applied in reverse, read under the base's own parse environment; joint_claim_join needs base-side records and the diff's two sides for its own join; behavioral_receipt_host needs one checked git invocation. None of that is the deleted wall's adjudication: no delta is computed here and no verdict is issued. WHY RUST RATHER THAN .dag: the input carrier is the host-only ModuleDeclarationRecord (gunbc.declaration_index_seed_growth CLASS A) and the acquisition is git over the object store, the scm lane's CLASS B boundary. THREE PROVENANCES, NOT ONE. (1) RENAMED CARRYOVER: every declaration from KERNEL_DECLARATION_IDENTITY through kernel_set_serves_both existed in namespace_wave_admission.rs on main, admitted under the wall's own justification, and moved unchanged when that module was deleted -- except kernel_set_serves_both, whose body the kernel-set repair below rewrote. (2) THE KERNEL-SET READER, NEW SEMANTIC SURFACE: KERNEL_TYPES_ITEM, kernel_names_at and as_kernel_set_refusal were added when kernel_set_serves_both stopped comparing the whole dag/std/types.dag blob (a byte proxy that refused every edit to that file) and began comparing the base revision's evaluated kernel_type_set names to this binary's. (3) SHARED EXTRACTIONS: evaluate_owned_item_in, closure_paths_of and revision_scratch_root were lifted out of evaluate_environment_in, environment_closure_paths and load_parse_environment_with_closure in that same change so the kernel reader reuses the environment loader's route instead of copying it; they add no behaviour of their own.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "The reconstruction and the selector follow gunbc.declaration_index_seed_growth's first step: when the per-module declaration record is a .dag carrier, these are ordinary folds over it. The git and revision-materialization legs follow the scm lane: a typed repository-read transport supplying a file's text at a ref dissolves git_stdout, diff_sides, materialize_revision_paths and the environment loader's acquisition half. The environment decode dissolves when the parse environment is a typed value the toolchain hands to its consumers rather than a value this binary re-derives by evaluation. The kernel-set reader (kernel_names_at, as_kernel_set_refusal, KERNEL_TYPES_ITEM) dissolves when the base reconstruction carries distinct base and head kernel sets from versioned declaration facts, so no revision's set is re-derived by evaluation and no single compiled-in set is consulted for both sides.",
  current_boundary: "Reachable from the required floor's planning row (run_required_floor, witnesses lane; the kernel-set reader only when dag/std/types.dag differs between base and head), the joint_claim_join bin, behavioral_receipt_host's git leg, and tests/parse_environment_decode_roundtrip.rs. Computes no delta and decides no verdict: the wave-admission adjudication that consumed this machinery is deleted, and no caller here can refuse a merge over a namespace change."
}
